## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/block_begin.html
- Summary (EN): Marks the start of a block and defines the inputs that feed it. The block can run inline when inputs are wired into this node, or externally through an Invoke Block COP.
- Résumé (FR) : Ouvre un bloc réutilisable et déclare ses entrées, qui le font tourner en ligne ou par un Invoke Block COP.

- Inputs meaning: ["Block inputs: a list whose length is set by Block Inputs, each with a name and a type; the page does not document a fixed port order"]

- Key parameters: ["Block Path: path to the Block End COP that closes the block; it must be at the same network level", "Rename Wires Using Output Labels: output wire names come from port labels when on, otherwise they pass through from the inputs", "Block Inputs: number of inputs to the block", "Input Name: identifies each input when invoking the block or binding inputs for slap comp", "Input Type: kind of data each input accepts and can connect to"]

- Caveats: ["Time Shift nodes cannot be used inside a block when they require block inputs at different times", "Workaround: place a Time Pack before Block Begin and wire the result in as a cable", "Enabling output-label renaming discards incoming wire names"]

